{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785183895,"nonce":"IUg1G3iEu62qDDwiW4NXq6jtqMw=","title":"ADR-0062 s2: the change set is the overlay upper layer — exact, not inferred","message":"An `overlayfs` upper directory contains **precisely** the paths a Step touched, put there by the kernel. Turn an upper directory into a change set a drain can build a snapshot from.\n\nThe difficulty is that an upper layer is not just \"files that changed\": a deletion is a **character device with rdev 0:0** (a whiteout), a wholesale directory replacement is a directory carrying the `trusted.overlay.opaque=\"y\"` xattr, and a rename leaves a `trusted.overlay.redirect`. Reading `trusted.*` needs `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`.\n\nSplit so the tricky part is testable everywhere: a **pure classifier** over `(file type, rdev, opaque xattr)` → verdict, plus a **walk** that gathers those facts, plus one Linux-and-privilege-gated integration test over a real overlay.\n\n\n- [ ] Added, modified, deleted (whiteout) and opaque-directory cases all classified correctly, with the reasoning in comments\n- [ ] Deletions and opaque directories are modelled explicitly — a caller never has to guess\n- [ ] An unsupported `trusted.overlay.redirect` **fails loudly**; silently mishandling a rename means publishing a snapshot that omits a file\n- [ ] An upper containing nothing yields an empty change set (an untouched Step publishes no diff)\n- [ ] Hashes nothing and does not touch the CAS — this slice answers only \"what changed\"\n- [ ] The gated integration test **panics** when opted in and the capability is missing, never `return`s (regression guard for commit `505f313`)\n\n\nNone - can start immediately (pairs with s1 but does not depend on it)","files":null}]}